  "response_text": "Here's what I can help with using the tools on this MCP server:\n\n- **Tool registry management & inspection** — list tools, read tool definitions, check registration/approval status, register, update, or abort tools.\n- **System/robot state inspection** — read proprioceptive state, lidar scans, perceived scene, camera frames, and server info.\n- **Planning & control** — plan actions, execute manipulation/physical actions, emit control commands, publish ROS2/twist commands.\n- **Authorization decisions** — check whether an action is allowed or denied for a subject.\n- **General queries** — local time, weather, and temperature.\n\nSteps I would take for the task I was given (\"review the tools registered on my MCP server and tell me their current state\"):\n\n1. Call `get_server_info` to learn the server name, version, and the number of tools registered and approved.\n2. Call `list_tools` to enumerate every tool and its approval status.\n3. For each tool returned, call `read_tool_metadata` to retrieve its registered definition (name, description, schema, approval status).\n4. Compare each tool's registration state and approval state, noting any that are registered but not approved or whose definitions look inconsistent or modified.\n5. Compile a per-tool summary of current state (registered/approved, name, description) and report any anomalies.",
